            </div>
          </div>

          <p>
            There are catches. The subscription price is not locked: the price can change between the day you subscribe and the day an order ships, and the discount applies to the price at that time. Amazon emails you before each delivery, so glance at the price then. You can skip a delivery or cancel at any time, which makes it easy to avoid a pile of tubs if your training changes.
          </p>

          <p>
            Our rule of thumb: subscribe only to a product and flavor you have already finished at least once, set the frequency to slightly longer than you need, and bring the date forward if you run low. That avoids paying for a large tub you do not like, and it avoids stockpiling powder that sits past its best-before date.
          </p>
